{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Let the maiden to whom I say, 'Please tip your pitcher.'</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said: three asked in an unfit manner — to two He answered fitly, and to one He answered unfitly. And these are they: Eliezer servant of Abraham, and Saul son of Kish, and Jephthah the Gileadite. Eliezer servant of Abraham, as it is written: ״והיה הנערה אשר אומר אליה״ and so forth — perhaps even a lame woman, even a blind one? The Holy One, blessed be He, prepared for him Rebekah. Saul son of Kish, as it is written (1 Samuel 17:25): ״והיה האיש אשר יכנו יעשרנו המלך עושר גדול ואת בתו יתן לו״ — perhaps even a slave, even a bastard? The Holy One, blessed be He, prepared for him David. Jephthah the Gileadite, as it is written (Judges 11:31): ״והיה היוצא אשר יצא מדלתי ביתי החוצה והעליתיהו עולה״ — perhaps even an unclean thing? The Holy One, blessed be He, prepared for him his daughter. And this is what the prophet said to Israel (Jeremiah 8:22): ״הצרי אין בגלעד אם רופא אין שם״; and it is written (ibid. 19): ״אשר לא צויתי ולא דברתי ולא עלתה על לבי״." "<b>You have shown to Your servant, for Isaac.</b> She is fitting for him, for she performs deeds of kindness and is fit to enter the household of Abraham." "<b>And by it I shall know.</b> It is the language of supplication: inform me now that You have done kindness with my master."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text appears to duplicate the Saul prooftext and citation before the Jephthah section; the Saul entry cites 1 Samuel 17:25 and then the same citation is repeated before Jephthah's own prooftext from Judges 11:31 — translated faithfully as the text stands, including the duplication. The citation for Jephthah's prooftext (שופטים י״א:ל״א) and Jeremiah citations (ירמיהו ח׳:כ״ב and ibid. 19) normalized."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:44.673456918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}